  "query_preview": "..It'a beautiful day across the CWA with\ntemperatures 10-12 degrees below normal and sunny to partly\ncloudy skies. Aloft, a closed low is moving through the Four\nCorners region and an east-west oriented ridge is building into\nthe upper Great Basin and Pacific Northwest. The closed low \nwill be absorbed by a trough moving in from Canada by Friday and\nthe ridge will build into western Wyoming and Colorado pinching\noff a closed low that will sit over southern California and \nnorthern Baja. At the same time a very strong surface high forms\njust east of the Rockies centered over Wyoming and gradually \nmoves south Friday into Saturday. This surface high will be very\nstrong with NAEFS mean MSLP 3 standard deviations above \naverage. This will create a very strong pressure gradient over \nsoutheast Arizona leading to a long-duration easterly wind \nevent Thursday night into Saturday. \n\nNAEFS mean 850 mb wind speeds are 40-50 kts late Thursday night\ninto Friday night, which is 4-6 standard deviations above \nnormal. Expect surface winds starting around 16/06Z through \nSaturday afternoon to be 30-45 mph with gusts 50-70 mph. Models \nshow the strongest winds in the lee of Sky Islands, likely \nenhanced by mountain waves and downsloping. Thanks to the \nposition of the closed low over Baja 700-500 mb winds will be \nout of the southeast, so momentum transfer down to the surface \nwill have a similar direction to the surface, which is not \ntypical for east wind events. Also, to drive home how anomalous \nthis is the Euro EFI is at 0.95-1.0 for most of southeast \nArizona Friday. REFS wind gust probabilities for 60 mph or \ngreater Friday are 30-90 percent for a good portion of southeast\nArizona with the highest probabilities in the lee of the \nmountains and east-west oriented valleys.\n\nBased on model guidance and growing confidence in how anomalous\nthis event will be the Wind Advisory has been upgraded to a High\nWind Warning from 11 PM Thursday through 11 PM Friday from\ncentral Pima County eastward. A Wind Advisory will then be in \neffect from 11 PM Friday through Saturday afternoon. The\nTohono O'odham Nation has also been added to the Wind Advisory\nstarting early Friday morning. In the High Wind Warning area \nexpect sustained speeds 35-45 mph with gusts 55-70 mph. Best \ntiming for the strongest winds looks to be Friday morning and \nearly afternoon. These winds could lead to downed trees and \npower poles as well as blowing dust. High profile vehicles \nshould also use caution when driving in cross winds.\n\nIn the tropics Hurricane Simon is 250 miles south southeast of \nCabo and will weaken and move northwestward over southern Baja \nthis weekend into early next week. This will send moisture into \nsouthern Arizona leading to a chance for showers and \nthunderstorms Friday into Saturday. Initially best chances will \nbe west of Tucson then cover most of southeast Arizona Saturday.\nSunday will likely see a brief break in rain chances, but the \nupper air pattern stays fairly progressive. By Sunday the closed\nlow over Baja opens up and flattens out as a Pacific low \napproaches the Northwest and then moves down the west coast \nearly to mid next week. This will lead to continued below normal\ntemperatures and 20-40 PoPs.",
